hypotheses.statement:
Let $1\leq q\leq n$, and let $f_1,\ldots,f_N$ be convergent power series near $0\in\mathbb C^q$. Suppose that a vector $\lambda\in\mathbb R_{>0}^q$ makes a specified exponent $e_j$ the unique minimum of $\lambda\cdot\alpha$ on the support of $f_j$, and let $c_j\ne0$ be its coefficient. For any $\gamma_j\in\mathbb Z^{n-q}$, as $s\downarrow0$ the functions $$\label{eq:weighted-limit}
 c_j^{-1}s^{-\lambda\cdot e_j}
 f_j(s^{\lambda_1}Z_1,\ldots,s^{\lambda_q}Z_q)U^{\gamma_j}
 \longrightarrow Z^{e_j}U^{\gamma_j}$$ converge locally uniformly on $\mathbb C^q\times\mathbb T^{n-q}$, with all derivatives of any fixed finite order. The assertion means that each fixed compact set is in the domain of the left-hand side for all sufficiently small $s>0$. When $q=n$, the unchanged variable block is omitted.

